WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:09.670
Explosive Shoot

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.810
Keep fighting chasing your dream

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.140
with love, courage and friendship

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.640
This Blade and I are one

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.680
Spin as hard as you can until the limit

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.780
BURNING SOUL

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.200
The things I can't do alone

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.140
are not impossible if you're with me

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.960
Come with me

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.280
to the ends of this world

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:03.540
The Four Sacred Beasts are athletes of love

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.100
Shine! Open your eyes!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.730
Dragoon  Dranzer  Draciel  Driger

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.450
Awaken!

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.060
Fly across the sky, my energy

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.380
Rise up, Sacred Beast!

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.830
To defeat all the enemies who stand in our way

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.050
jump, bearing everyone's hopes

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.080
SHINING SOUL

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.500
We are very sorry for making you wait so long, Ralf-sama.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:42.590
Since this project is on an unprecedented
scale, we made sure to be extremely careful.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.700
From there, our schedule grew and grew...

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.490
Enough with the excuses. Hurry up and show me.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.300
Yes, my mistake.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.460
Ah, there it is!

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:55.720
<i>That</i> is the Bey stadium our company went all-out on.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.570
We call it the Jurgens Stadium.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:04.040
It features a capacity of 100,000 seats, for both
the public and for VIPs, as well as an orchestra pit.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.940
Not to mention the world's biggest TV screen.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:10.860
We've followed your instructions to a T, Ralf-sama.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:16.530
This will become a new holy ground for
Bladers and Beyblade enthusiasts across the world.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:24.170
The Strongest Euro Team is Formed!

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.430
Is that serve all you've got?

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:34.440
Tch!

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.610
Tennis is boring. How about we play something else?

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:49.130
Welcome back, Ralf. How's the new stadium shaping up?

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:52.980
Can't complain. I'm sure you guys will love it, too.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.400
Ralf-sama!

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.840
It's an emergency!

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:03.160
They've been at it for two hours now!

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:06.590
They've been eating without pause since morning.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:10.260
At this rate, our mansion's food reserves will vanish!

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:14.140
Locusts! They're all but locusts!

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.740
Yum, yum!

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.450
Ralf.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:20.940
You're <i>still</i> here?

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:26.150
While I did offer you rooms for the night,
you're beginning to overstay your welcomes.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.000
Well, by the time Takao woke up,
he said he was too hungry to move, so...

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:35.900
So we couldn't help but have <i>breakfast</i>,
and it tasted too good to stop.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.800
That's not what I'd asked.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.690
In any case, leave as soon as you're done.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:43.450
Johann, prepare the car.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:43.910
Yes, sir.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.120
Not leavin'.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:45.760
What?!

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.730
We're not leaving.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:51.300
We're not moving an inch
until we get to fight you guys.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:52.760
What do you mean?

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.420
Last night, we came to a conclusion.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:00.380
We will fight against you as a team.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.680
Are you awake, Takao?

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.600
I can't even sleep.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.280
Kai just... lost.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:15.910
That's it.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.070
I'll challenge them to a fight!

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:19.740
Rei!

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.240
If we leave things like this,
we'll live the rest of our lives sleepless.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.910
I'm up for it, too. I fight for the BBA <i>team</i>!

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.660
Alright, that's the spirit!

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.520
Let's join forces and blow 'em away!

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:37.770
Very well.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:40.680
We've come too far to turn back now.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:48.940
Foolish!

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.550
As a team, eh?

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.640
Beaten black and blue and you still don't get it?

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:58.930
Have you forgotten Ralf's principle of
never fighting the same opponents twice?

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.340
That's fine by me.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:04.280
Then our principle is to stay
right here and eat until you'll face us.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:05.530
What?!

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.260
Sounds about right.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:10.260
The clock is ticking, ya know!

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.700
And you, Johann!

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:16.120
Bring me some lotus roots with mustard and tuna natto.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.510
And for dessert, some almond jelly.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.820
Ah, Johann. I want a hamburger and potatoes.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.150
Sounds good to me.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.170
Pay for these sins with your defeat!

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.730
Fire Rod!

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:46.210
Suzaku!

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.080
You'll see!

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.970
Not bad, Kai.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:03.890
<i>Nice training</i>.

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:05.000
You guys...

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.360
You're awful, Kai.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.930
How could you sneak out on us to train?

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:12.500
This is <i>my</i> fight.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.240
It doesn't involve you.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:17.260
You think so? It has a lot to do with us.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:22.320
This time we really need you, Kai,
or else we'll be one down to them.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:23.600
What?!

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.410
We asked Ralf's group to fight us as a team.

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:29.070
You did what?!

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:30.740
How's it sound?

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.260
Say, Kai... Will you battle against me?

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.970
Me? Battle with you?

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:39.300
All-out, no holds barred.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:43.550
Or maybe you lost your fighting
spirit with the shock of yesterday's defeat?

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:44.910
Oh, shut it.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.220
Nice to hear.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:53.620
Yes, now's as good a time as any.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:56.350
We need training data unmistakable from field data.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.860
Go... Shoot!

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:02.010
Dragoon!

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:02.940
Dranzer!

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:17.650
Looks like they actually plan on taking back the title.

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:20.300
Seriously, how naive can they be?

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.990
Are they naive, though?

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:28.840
At any rate, last night, you used your
secret technique—Fire Rod—against Kai.

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:33.880
Since I first met them, I've been thinking...

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:37.510
Some aspect feels off whenever I fight them.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.790
What is that aspect?

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.540
I plan on finding out.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:46.940
Ralf, why don't you accept their challenge?

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.840
Hey, now. What's gotten into you?!

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:54.010
Are you saying we shoud actually fight them?!

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:55.370
What's wrong with that?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.210
It could be surprisingly fun.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:58.330
Foolish.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:00.410
Well, Ralf?

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.210
Aren't you forgetting something super important?

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:09.420
If we accept their challenge,
we'll have to fight <i>as a team</i>.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:14.090
They want us to fight as a team,
and be all friendly and stuff.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.140
Can you do that? Huh?!

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:18.730
There's nothing to see in them.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:24.270
The power of their Beys, the way they
control Sacred Beasts... They're third-class.

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:27.290
You've been influenced by them.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:29.420
And like a virus, you've been infected.

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.860
That's my Ralf! Speaks the truth...

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:38.120
However, now that you've been
infected, treatment is necessary.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:42.750
Johann.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.210
Bring them to the inner garden.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.640
I have something to tell you.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.650
Consider your challenge accepted.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:58.340
Ralf!

00:08:58.840 --> 00:08:59.720
Really?

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.730
However, this will be an exhibition match.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.680
Exit-bishop match? What's that?

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:11.280
It's a non-title match. Instead of a serious battle,
it's more of a performance, for entertainment's sake.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.980
The opening ceremony for my
newly-constructed stadium is fast approaching.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:22.320
For one of its programs, we will have
you fight us for our guests' amusement.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:25.680
Frankly, you'll be cannon fodder.

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:27.820
C-Cannon fodder?!

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:32.850
The fight will be a 3v3, but each
match will consist of a single set.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.880
Surely this will be able to cure you.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.770
W-Wait a minute...

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:40.330
Ralf, what's gotten into you?!

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:43.110
You said you didn't fight
the same opponents twice!

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:46.170
I did, but this is an exhibition match.

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:48.200
It's not a true battle.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:49.040
Ralf...

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:50.860
If you don't like it, then leave.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:53.690
Make sure to train hard.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:58.160
If you go down too easily,
our guests will be disappointed.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:03.170
Bring it on! Either way, it's a deal!

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.700
We can fight again.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.550
This time I won't hold back.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:09.630
Heck yeah, that's what I'm lookin' for!

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.290
W-Whoa!

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:42.870
So this is Ralf's new stadium...

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:47.920
According to my calculations, it's three
times bigger than the Battle Dome in America!

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:50.240
You can tell it's brand-new.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:52.870
That fresh smell is still in the air.

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:54.960
Brand-new...

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:56.590
Takao?

00:10:57.540 --> 00:11:00.350
First!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.810
Now, let's see... First!

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.690
Wait, this is only a rug.

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.900
Why's it lying around?

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:14.970
Long time no see.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.060
My name is Blood.

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:20.280
Apostle of darkness, wandering in search of blood.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:22.640
Why are <i>you</i> here?!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.160
I came to see my future sacrifices.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.040
Sacrifices?

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:32.550
Your group or Ralf's... Whoever wins
will become the prey of Team Shadow.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:33.970
What's that?!

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:37.340
This battle will separate the
strong Sacred Beasts from the weak.

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:42.010
By defeating the strongest Sacred
Beasts, we will be relieved of our curse.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:46.940
Now go battle for the honor of becoming our sacrifices.

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:58.800
I'm looking forward to seeing who wins.

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:04.740
Team Shadow is here?

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:08.290
He said they'll prey on whoever wins.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.330
Interesting. Let's give them a run for their money!

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:17.010
Anyway, rather than worrying over Team
Shadow, we should focus on the battle ahead.

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:20.560
The fight will be a 3v3.
We need to decide who's playing.

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:25.140
Me, obviously. I'm the one who needs to get back at Ralf.

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:29.680
I'll fight, too. I can't turn down any strong opponents.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.550
Then, for our final pick...

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:36.650
<i>Good luck</i>, Kai.

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.930
This time, you have to win.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:40.690
Max...

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:44.660
The game is on!

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.660
Alright! Let's show those guys our true power!

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:50.170
Yeah!

00:12:58.020 --> 00:12:59.410
Wow...

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:00.430
Look at that.

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:07.600
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:11.400
Welcome to the Jurgens Stadium
Opening Exhibition Match!

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:14.400
Hey, why the heck are <i>you</i> here?!

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:17.530
Where there's a Bey battle, there's DJ!

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:21.070
Here in the world's biggest stadium,

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:27.420
the fierce battle between the BBA team and
the Elite Bladers of Europe is about to begin!

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.290
Everybody, are you ready?

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:38.670
Of course! Leave it to the world's best and
brightest! Silence is a way of showing excitement!

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:40.930
I'm getting even more fired up!

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:41.940
Heck yeah!

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:44.000
He doesn't let anything get him down.
Heck yeah!

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:47.300
DJ looks like the only one who's fired up.

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:50.000
Then let me introduce our players!

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:53.810
Following their victory in
America, they've invaded Europe!

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:56.160
It's the BBA team!

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:01.730
And now, what you've all been waiting for...
Elites by birth, Bladers by choice,

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:03.240
they've arrived!

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:10.080
This is the legendary Euro team!

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:12.120
Bravo! Bravo!

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:13.540
Euro team?

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:14.720
I knew it.

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:18.680
They're the best four of
the recent European Tournament.

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:24.580
As such, they were supposed to represent
Europe at the World Tournament's finals.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.170
The winner is Ralf!

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:34.220
The winner of the Beyblade Battle European Tournament is Ralf Jurgens from Germany!

00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:38.770
Johnny McGregor of the UK comes in second.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:45.360
Olivier Polanger of France and Giancarlo
Tornatore of Italy are tied for third place.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:50.920
These four are going to take on the
World Tournament as the Euro team!

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:56.400
Euro team? This is the first time I've heard of it.

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:58.920
Forming a team with strangers? No thanks.

00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:01.750
Beyblade is a solo sport.

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.420
Why do we need to team up, exactly?

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:07.170
We refuse to form the Euro team!

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:15.320
Holy cow! They just refused
to join forces as the Euro team!

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:17.950
So that's what happened...

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:23.160
This explains why none of them were
going to participate in the Tournament.

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:30.010
A team is a group created by weak individuals
to compensate for a lack of strength.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.750
We don't need any of that.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:35.620
And that's what we're here to show you.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:40.910
Bring it on! We'll show you
just how strong our BBA team is!

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:42.760
Do your best, Takao!

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:44.500
You bet! Leave it to me!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:45.710
Wait, huh?

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:48.210
Professor, where'd you go?

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.220
I'm up here!

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:51.520
Professor!

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:53.860
What're you doing up there?

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:56.070
Well, y-you see...

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:57.470
Team Shadow!

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.320
You're holding the Professor hostage again?!

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:01.860
Do not worry.

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.980
We didn't kidnap him.

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:07.700
We plan on watching the fight with him, that's all.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.450
Watching the fight?

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:10.900
Team Shadow..?

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.580
It's been a while, Ralf.

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:15.820
Don't tell me you've forgotten who I am.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:17.210
I have.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:20.120
And even if I did remember you, so what?

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:22.430
Ralf! Why, you..!

00:16:22.430 --> 00:16:25.540
Johnny! I'm here to witness your defeat!

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.920
Olivier, even if you win this battle...

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.770
Giancarlo! When the time comes, I will finish you myself!

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:37.650
Anyway... do your best, guys!

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.030
7 of Diamonds.

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:45.310
9 of Clovers.

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:46.930
Queen of Hearts.

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:48.460
Ace of Spades.

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:51.980
Olivier will go first. Giancarlo, you're out.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:53.660
Ah, dang it.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:55.660
Whoever it is, hurry on over.

00:16:58.510 --> 00:17:00.990
I'll fall asleep if I wait much longer.

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:04.410
You're as boorish as ever.

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:09.000
Very well. I shall wake you up with an artistic battle.

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:13.210
The first set will consist of Olivier and Rei's fight!

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:15.470
Players, to the shooting points!

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:21.640
It's finally starting!

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.070
We're in your hands, Rei! End this, quickly!

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:26.060
Players, are you ready?

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:29.320
Three, Two, One!

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:32.410
Go... Shoot!

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:43.960
Driger!

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:45.190
Unicolyon!

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.150
Go, Unicolyon!

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:07.280
Wow! Unicolyon's violent rotation
is making the whole stadium tremble!

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.110
Be careful, Rei!

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:12.160
Unicolyon's tactic is to take away your balance!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.950
I'm already aware of that. Endure, Driger!

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:20.180
Elegant appearance, elegant sprint,

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:23.490
and this is my elegant attack!

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:27.080
Driger, tackle him!

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:31.710
Driger stopped Unicolyon's attack!

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:32.930
No way!

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:34.260
Good job, Rei!

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:36.340
Don't make light of Byakko's power!

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:37.340
What?!

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:39.380
Driger!

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:43.150
Unicolyon!

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:47.730
That Olivier is even more powerful
than the one who defeated me!

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:51.720
Byakko's power has improved accordingly!

00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:53.940
We may actually win this battle!

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:58.920
Olivier, I know this is an exhibition match,
but aren't you holding back a little too much?

00:18:58.920 --> 00:18:59.780
No.

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:05.130
Olivier is going all-out, and he's
still being pushed back by that guy.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:08.700
<i>Go, go, go!</i>

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:10.050
Go, go, go!

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:13.970
Unicolyon has nowhere left to run!

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:18.320
This is it! This feeling!

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:21.320
This feeling of isolation, even in my homeland...

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.600
What <i>is</i> this?

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:27.220
This is the end!

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:28.810
Tiger Claw!

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:33.610
Don't get cocky!

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:40.990
W-What's going on?!

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:59.730
Both players are out of the stadium.

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:01.940
The first set ends in a tie!

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:05.230
So close!

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:06.730
He had almost won!

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.310
Olivier... tied?

00:20:11.570 --> 00:20:13.160
Thanks, Olivier.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:18.940
You were trying to put on a show to
make this battle more exciting, right?

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:22.660
Tell me I'm right.

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:24.620
You <i>still </i>don't get it?

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:25.660
What?!

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:29.430
I only managed to tie because I already knew them a little.

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:32.700
You better stop looking down on them like this,

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:34.720
or else you're going to regret it.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:44.930
I know them, too.

00:20:46.690 --> 00:20:49.390
Sorry, I had him cornered, and yet...

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:51.060
Don't worry, Rei.

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:55.360
It was a <i>nice fight!</i> Olivier looked really confused, too.

00:20:57.340 --> 00:21:02.460
With the first set ending in a tie, the
result of this battle is still up in the air!

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:06.910
The long awaited second set
will be between Johhny and Kai!

00:21:07.510 --> 00:21:09.290
Players, get on stage!

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.120
Kai!

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:14.290
Go get 'em.

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:17.550
You have your own battles to worry about.

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:26.510
That's right. I already know you all too well.

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:29.480
Is that right?

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:44.720
Spring waves its hand smiling,

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:50.200
Summer spreads passion.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:55.350
Seasons pass one after the other,

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:59.560
Fall and Winter are good friends.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.660
When there is a problem you can't solve,

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:11.560
Trust, friendship, love and emotion

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:18.800
Clouds keep flying across the sky,

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:24.200
the sky keeps changing every second

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:29.090
My eyes well up and tears stream down my face,

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:33.090
but they're not tears of sadness

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:39.420
I summon my courage and try to put it into words.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.770
"Let's go on a journey to the city of hope!"

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:49.760
All your dreams will come true

00:22:57.840 --> 00:23:02.990
According to my analysis,
the end of the European arc is here!

00:23:03.350 --> 00:23:05.930
Kai vs Johnny, Takao vs Ralf...

00:23:05.930 --> 00:23:11.160
These battles are so exciting, like "Wow!" "No way!" "Oh my goodness!"

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:13.080
And suddenly, a question for you.

00:23:13.080 --> 00:23:17.100
What is it that Ralf's group
doesn't have that Takao's group does?

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:20.160
Next time: Settle it! The Power to Win.

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:24.320
Holy cow! Finally, President Daitenji's big plan will be revealed!
